# This project is deployed and run on Ubuntu. Force LF line endings for anything that gets
# executed as a script or read by a shell/interpreter, regardless of core.autocrlf on whichever
# machine (Windows or otherwise) someone happens to be editing from - a CRLF shebang line
# ("#!/bin/bash\r") fails on Linux with "bad interpreter: No such file or directory" before the
# script even runs. This exact issue hit every .sh file in this repo on a Windows dev machine
# with core.autocrlf=true and no .gitattributes to override it.
*.sh text eol=lf
*.py text eol=lf
*.yml text eol=lf
*.yaml text eol=lf
*.properties text eol=lf
